+
+## Summary
+
+Staff can create a discount code with `POST /admin/discount-codes`, giving a whole-number percentage off from 1 to 100.
+Customers can pass an optional `discount_code` to `POST /checkout`, and that percentage comes off the items (not shipping).
+Each order stores its discount and the code used, and `GET /admin/orders/{id}` shows both.
+
+Decisions to flag in review:
+
+- **Free shipping is judged after the discount.** A £55 order with 10% off pays £49.50 for the items, so it no longer gets free shipping. Judging it on the subtotal before the discount instead would be a one-line change in `shop/pricing.py`.
+- **A code can take up to 100% off**, making the items free. The customer still pays shipping.
